Short:        NetBSD 11 TCP/IP stack for AmigaOS (bsdsocket)
Author:       zombu4 (https://github.com/zombu4)
Uploader:     zombu4 (https://github.com/zombu4)
Type:         comm/tcp
Version:      0.8.1
Architecture: m68k-amigaos >= 3.1.0
Requires:     68020+, Fast RAM, a SANA-II network driver
Distribution: NoCD

AmiBSDNet is a complete TCP/IP network stack for classic AmigaOS,
built from the networking code of the NetBSD 11 kernel - the real BSD
TCP/IP, IPv4 and IPv6 implementation - running on top of Exec.
Applications use the standard bsdsocket.library (AmiTCP / Roadshow
API), so existing network software works unchanged.

- NetBSD 11 TCP/IP: modern TCP (CUBIC, SACK, window scaling), UDP,
  ICMP, raw sockets, IPv4 and IPv6 in the kernel
- works with any SANA-II network driver
- DHCP client with lease renewal, or a fixed address
- DNS resolver, hosts file, getaddrinfo()
- runs entirely from Fast RAM; built for the PiStorm (Emu68), works on
  any 68020-68060
- Ethernet and Wi-Fi at the same time; Internet traffic follows the
  cable when one is plugged in
- Wi-Fi encryption included (WirelessManager, WPA/WPA2); on a PiStorm
  the Wi-Fi driver of your Emu68 (wifipi.device) is used as it is
- PaulaNET (Wi-Fi through the floppy port) used by itself whenever it
  is plugged in, hidden otherwise; the installer copies its driver from
  the adapter's disk and checks the copy (optional verification of the
  driver against the official releases)
- Workbench status icon and Exchange commodity: online/offline at a
  glance, double-click for details; Settings window for drivers,
  DHCP or fixed address, DNS and the Wi-Fi network, applied at once
- NetCtrl (status, online/offline, wait for network) and Ping
- SerialShell: a Shell on the serial port for a terminal on another
  computer (8N1, no handshaking, 19200 baud by default), switched on
  and off in the Settings window
- Installer for Workbench 3.2: finds the network adapters itself and
  offers to switch from another TCP/IP stack (Roadshow, Miami, AmiTCP,
  Genesis) as a trial: it comes back by itself if AmiBSDNet does not
  connect

Install: double-click "Install" in the AmiBSDNet drawer.

Source code and issue tracker: https://github.com/zombu4/AmiBSDNet

